(   - "The research team has published its findings.") Tj
T*
(   - British English: Permits both singular and plural concord depending on semantic intention) Tj
T*
(   \(notional concord\). If individual members act discordantly, plural verbs are preferred:) Tj
T*
(   - "The committee have disagreed on the allocation of research funds.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Contexts Requiring Plural Verbs:) Tj
T*
(   When members of a collective unit perform individual, disparate actions simultaneously, plural) Tj
T*
(   concord is mandated in both styles:) Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "The panel were divided in their evaluations of the clinical trial data.") Tj
T*
(   - Stylistic Revision: "The members of the panel were divided in their evaluations...") Tj
T*
(   \(eliminates ambiguity\).) Tj
