(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze prepositional collocations and idiomatic verb-preposition pairings in molecular biology and biochemistry.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Prepositional Collocation in Scientific Syntax:) Tj
T*
(   In academic English, specific verbs, nouns, and adjectives demand exact prepositional) Tj
T*
(   complements that cannot be substituted logically or translated literally:) Tj
T*
(   - Consist of: "The replisome consists of multiple catalytic enzymes." \(Not *consists out of\).) Tj
T*
(   - Adhere to: "Fibroblasts adhere to the collagen-coated substrate." \(Not *adhere on\).) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute for: "Synthetic nucleotides were substituted for natural bases." \(Not *substituted) Tj
T*
(   with\).) Tj
T*
(   - Comply with: "All protocols complied with international biosafety standards." \(Not *complied) Tj
T*
(   to\).) Tj
T*
(   - Correlate with: "Absorbance correlates directly with protein concentration." \(Not *correlates) Tj
T*
(   to\).) Tj
T*
(   - Deficient in: "The medium was deficient in essential amino acids." \(Not *deficient of\).) Tj
T*
(   - Susceptible to: "Gram-positive bacteria are susceptible to penicillin." \(Not *susceptible) Tj
T*
(   with\).) Tj
T*
(   - Incubate at / for: "Incubate at 37 deg C for 48 hours." \(Temperature takes 'at'; duration) Tj
T*
(   takes 'for'\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
